(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase456DuplicationDeadCodeAndUnwiredEradication"
  :createdAt 1789157400000
  :status "done"
  :priorityOrder 4
  :summary "Duplication, Dead Code and Unwired Eradication: remove the 371 redundant copies that the broken binder forced into existence, retire the dead and the stubbed, and give every unreachable module a recorded verdict."
  :phase "Phase456DuplicationDeadCodeAndUnwiredEradication"
  :baseline "Measured 2026-09-11: 291 names carry 371 redundant definitions, 129 of them across package boundaries; estimate-tokens exists 15 times, strip-quotes 10, calc-savings 8, strip-colon 6, extract-between 5; balance-delimiters was promoted to asl-parser and still has 2 survivors in harness; asl-codec/src/sh-transpile.asl:35 redefines escape-sh-arg while line 12 imports the canonical module. 14 definitions are referenced nowhere, 10 are stubs, 270 non test modules are never imported and never named outside their own file, and install.sh exists as four byte copies."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task45601"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-456"
      :title "Delete the 371 redundant copies now that importing works"
      :kind :remediation
      :lane "duplication"
      :state :planned
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789157400000
      :motivation "Phase452 was certified complete for exactly this work and no duplicate was removed: canonical copies were added beside the originals, so the measured effect was more duplication, not less. The reason the campaign failed is upstream. A module that cannot import cannot delegate, so every consumer had to carry its own copy, and instructing authors to import from asl-text while the binder silently drops unresolved imports produced files that declare the import, document the canonical use and still define the helper locally. Removal is safe only after Phase454."
      :purpose "Each duplicated name has one definition in the package D34 assigns it to, every other definition is deleted, and each consumer binds through a declared import that resolves. The count of redundant copies is recorded before and after."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["371 redundant copies reduced to a recorded residue with justification" "Every survivor is a justified local optimum under the two strikes rule, named individually" "asl-codec/src/sh-transpile.asl no longer shadows the module it imports"]
      :owns ["asl/packages/asl-codec/src" "asl/packages/asl-text/src" "asl/packages/asl-cli/src" "harness/src" "agent-core/src" "intel/src" "mem/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["estimate-tokens" "strip-quotes" "strip-colon" "extract-between" "calc-savings" "balance-delimiters" "escape-sh-arg"]
      :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "names"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D34" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45405"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45601"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45601.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Adding a second definition of a centralised name fails the check." "A file that both imports a module and redefines one of its exports fails." "A survivor without a recorded justification fails, so the residue cannot grow quietly."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45601" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Assign each duplicated name an owning package." "Delete duplicates and bind through imports." "Record and justify the residue." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task45602"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-456"
      :title "Retire the 14 definitions nothing references and the 10 stubs"
      :kind :remediation
      :lane "deadCode"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789157400000
      :motivation "14 definitions are referenced nowhere in the corpus and nowhere in any registry, manifest, script or document, among them make-svg-node in vdom/src/asn_svg.asl, which is the mock module Phase452 undertook to delete and did not. 10 definitions are stubs: 2 return a bare constant, including pin-input and pin-low in asl-arduino/src/gpio.asl, and 8 carry an unresolved marker. A stub that returns a constant is indistinguishable from a working function at every call site, which is how mock debt survives an audit that reads output rather than source."
      :purpose "Each of the 24 is deleted, or implemented, or declared unimplemented in a way that fails at the call site rather than returning a plausible constant. No definition survives in a state where calling it looks like success."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Dead definitions deleted" "Constant body stubs cannot masquerade as implementations" "Marker stubs resolved or converted to explicit failures"]
      :owns ["vdom/src" "asl-arduino/src" "asl/web/src" "asl/packages/asl-sql/src" "harness/src" "web-api-search/src" "agent-core/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["make-svg-node" "pin-input" "pin-low" "render-placeholder"]
      :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "gates"]
      :invariants ["C1" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45601"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45602"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45602.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A newly added function referenced by nothing is reported." "A function whose body is a bare constant is reported, and one that legitimately returns a constant is exempted only by an explicit declaration." "Calling a declared unimplemented function fails rather than returning a value."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45602" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Confirm each of the 14 against the rebuilt reference graph." "Delete or implement." "Convert stubs to explicit failures." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task45603"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-456"
      :title "A verdict for each of the 270 unreachable modules"
      :kind :remediation
      :lane "deadCode"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789157400000
      :motivation "270 non test modules are imported by nobody and named nowhere outside their own file: 48 under asl, 28 under mem, 25 under agent, 18 under voice, 13 under agent-core, 12 each under intel, pack and agent-bus. Some of this is measurement artefact from the broken binder and will shrink once resolution is real; the rest is a body of code that is maintained, audited, counted in every density statistic and never executed. Until each has a verdict the project cannot say what it actually ships."
      :purpose "Every module is wired, deleted, or recorded as deliberately dormant with the condition that would wake it. The dormant set is a declared list, not a residue, and it is excluded from the density and coverage statistics that currently include it."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Each of the 270 carries wired, deleted or dormant" "Dormant modules are declared and excluded from statistics" "The subsystem disposition question for voice, agent, browser-plugin and crawler is answered by evidence"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/dependency-boundaries.asn" ".asl/mem/components.asn" "voice" "agent" "browser-plugin" "crawler"]
      :targetSymbols ["dependency-boundaries"]
      :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D34" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
